# Build output paths and the size each may reach before the `builds` tool
# deletes it whole for the next build to refill (cargo mostly from sccache).
# scripts/build-layout.sh, run first by the hooks and scripts/check.sh, links
# each path to /Volumes/Builds/coven/<checkout>/<path>, deletes the build
# copies in it that no build has used for three days (the tool's default), and
# then applies the caps. The hooks and scripts run cargo through
# scripts/cargo.sh, which records each build copy cargo uses, rebuilt or up to
# date.
#
# Caps are about twice a fresh build of each; target's is set by the
# `--all-features` test runs of the six crates, which reached 30-34G in one
# checkout (2026-11-04), so a cap below that deleted it whole on every run. target-ra is rust-analyzer's own:
# the Claude Code session's rust-analyzer (agent-instructions' rust-analyzer
# plugin) builds build scripts and proc macros there with
# `cargo check --workspace`. Its cap is a guess until a first build there is
# measured.
#
# path                     cap
target                     45G
target-ra                  6G
spec/proofs/io/.lake       1G
spec/proofs/merge/.lake    1G
spec/proofs/queue/.lake    1G
spec/proofs/sequence/.lake 1G
spec/proofs/storage/.lake  1G
